{:edb/db-before-t 1698 :edb/db-after-t 1699 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535011 50 #inst "2026-10-08T14:19:15.704Z" 13194139535011 true] [17592186105832 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326493 13194139535011 true] [17592186105832 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326500 13194139535011 true] [17592186105832 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326521 13194139535011 true] [17592186105832 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326535 13194139535011 true] [17592186105833 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326507 13194139535011 true] [17592186105833 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326511 13194139535011 true] [17592186105833 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326514 13194139535011 true] [17592186105833 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326528 13194139535011 true] [17592186105834 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326518 13194139535011 true] [17592186105834 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326542 13194139535011 true] [17592186105834 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326549 13194139535011 true] [17592186105834 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326556 13194139535011 true] [17592186326493 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326494 13194139535011 true] [17592186326493 1089 "q-128421" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326493 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535011 true] [17592186326493 1100 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $p=⟨2,2,3⟩,$ $q=⟨4,2,-1⟩,$ and $r=⟨-5,0,3⟩.$" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326493 1113 #uuid "9c59800e-2701-5f60-8d3e-288359179eb7" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326493 1145 "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot 3-0\\cdot (-1))-2(4\\cdot 3-(-5)\\cdot (-1))+3(4\\cdot 0-(-5)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =12-14+30 \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|28|=28.\n$$" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326494 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326495 13194139535011 true] [17592186326494 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326496 13194139535011 true] [17592186326494 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326497 13194139535011 true] [17592186326494 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326498 13194139535011 true] [17592186326494 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326499 13194139535011 true] [17592186326494 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535011 true] [17592186326494 1041 "selection" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326494 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326495 13194139535011 true] [17592186326494 1110 #uuid "5a574109-36b8-5949-9b70-4eeaf13c2197" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326495 1034 "28" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326495 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326495 1111 #uuid "22e964b6-4cdd-56c8-b63d-95b29bec5809" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326496 1034 "14" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326496 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326496 1111 #uuid "5ac9f39d-1e76-5ac0-ae9b-161f2e81b5cc" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326497 1034 "56" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326497 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326497 1111 #uuid "d689606a-b1d6-5a47-96a7-8235a9f0c345" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326498 1034 "42" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326498 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326498 1111 #uuid "c1f97eb6-6e15-5c61-a786-93ddc8911b49" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326499 1034 "4" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326499 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326499 1111 #uuid "91517ee9-d156-547e-8050-cdec91a0f02e" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326500 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326501 13194139535011 true] [17592186326500 1089 "q-18259" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326500 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535011 true] [17592186326500 1100 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-3,3,1⟩$, $b=⟨2,-1,3⟩$ and $c=⟨0,4,1⟩.$" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326500 1113 #uuid "fc223040-3a37-576b-a678-9d3b00321dab" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326500 1145 "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3((-1)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3)-3(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 3)+(2\\cdot 4-0\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =39-6+8 \\\\  & =41\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|41|=41.\n$$" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326501 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326502 13194139535011 true] [17592186326501 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326503 13194139535011 true] [17592186326501 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326504 13194139535011 true] [17592186326501 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326505 13194139535011 true] [17592186326501 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326506 13194139535011 true] [17592186326501 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535011 true] [17592186326501 1041 "selection" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326501 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326502 13194139535011 true] [17592186326501 1110 #uuid "3f1ae912-933b-5c96-971e-c28e417ab097" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326502 1034 "41" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326502 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326502 1111 #uuid "673cae1d-eb32-571c-b27a-757d2ebd1e59" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326503 1034 "15" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326503 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326503 1111 #uuid "d4abd956-3995-5eb0-9bf2-c9c45b45d748" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326504 1034 "32" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326504 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326504 1111 #uuid "e25bf302-b77e-57bd-8563-b8e1ff3e6927" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326505 1034 "35" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326505 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326505 1111 #uuid "2f4b2da7-fc1c-5d45-b5d1-66c133668f5e" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326506 1034 "53" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326506 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326506 1111 #uuid "c4bf8f1b-bae9-5ea5-9fe5-ca22e4d3cea9" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326507 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326508 13194139535011 true] [17592186326507 1089 "q-275353" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326507 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535011 true] [17592186326507 1100 "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨-2,1,-3⟩$, $b=⟨-1,k,2⟩$, and $c=⟨3,-2,4⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326507 1113 #uuid "bd47ad71-726b-598c-9cd8-8f7ef7e44966" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326507 1145 "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|+(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & k \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(k\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot 2)-((-1)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 2)-3((-1)\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot k) \\\\  & =-8k-8+10-6+9k \\\\  & =k-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ k-4 & =0 \\\\ k & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=4.$" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326509 13194139535011 true] [17592186326508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326510 13194139535011 true] [17592186326508 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535011 true] [17592186326508 1041 "field-1" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326508 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326509 13194139535011 true] [17592186326508 1110 #uuid "d0cd9b70-e2f1-54e9-9ff7-5f2bc5f704cd" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326509 1034 "4" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326509 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326509 1111 #uuid "13659ae6-e567-53cb-9aab-761952bceac9" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326510 1034 "5" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326510 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326510 1111 #uuid "5b76fa60-842d-5b16-8204-99b6ff005fc8" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326511 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326512 13194139535011 true] [17592186326511 1089 "q-280720" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326511 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535011 true] [17592186326511 1100 "Find $k$ given that the vectors $x=⟨2,0,k⟩$, $y=⟨1,4,3⟩$, and $z=⟨0,2,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326511 1113 #uuid "d369a6bd-35ca-5c57-9419-5c24b72446a0" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326511 1145 "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & k \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|+k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(4\\cdot 5-3\\cdot 2)+0+k(1\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2(20-6)+2k \\\\  & =28+2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =0 \\\\ 28+2k & =0 \\\\ 2k & =-28 \\\\ k & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-14.$" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326512 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326513 13194139535011 true] [17592186326512 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535011 true] [17592186326512 1041 "field-1" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326512 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326513 13194139535011 true] [17592186326512 1110 #uuid "6ddc02b8-3a95-5c91-b1c2-e5d366fdbe06" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326513 1034 "-14" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326513 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326513 1111 #uuid "bcdef9cd-da53-54f7-b9b4-1dc1d0848e2c" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326514 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326515 13194139535011 true] [17592186326514 1089 "q-280722" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326514 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535011 true] [17592186326514 1100 "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨1,3,0⟩$, $b=⟨0,4,2⟩$, and $c=⟨2,k,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326514 1113 #uuid "875a18b4-72a0-591f-b9da-03167f35bd1b" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326514 1145 "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\na\\cdot (b\\times c)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k & 5\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ k & 5\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 5-2\\cdot k)-3(0\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 2)=(20-2k)+12 \\\\  & =32-2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 32-2k & =0 \\\\ -2k & =-32 \\\\ k & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=16.$" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326515 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326516 13194139535011 true] [17592186326515 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326517 13194139535011 true] [17592186326515 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535011 true] [17592186326515 1041 "field-1" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326515 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326516 13194139535011 true] [17592186326515 1110 #uuid "e414834f-173d-5fbb-bb6a-4f2a12084f4b" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326516 1034 "16" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326516 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326516 1111 #uuid "bf549120-6114-5feb-b848-f01439d29d99" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326517 1034 "15" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326517 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535011 true] [17592186326517 1111 #uuid "45d1db52-a301-5925-a6a6-997e7f782f4c" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326518 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326519 13194139535011 true] [17592186326518 1089 "q-281025" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326518 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535011 true] [17592186326518 1100 "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(3,0,2),$ $B(5,1,3),$ $C(4,3,5),$ and $D(3,0,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326518 1113 #uuid "0731c398-d5f2-578b-97ec-94db7b1c6288" 13194139535011 true] [17592186326518 1145 "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(5i+1j+3k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =2i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(4i+3j+5k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =i+3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨1,3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i+5k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =3k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(3\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 0)-1(1\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 0)+1(1\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2(9)-1(3)+1(0) \\\\  & =18-3+0 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV